allows developers to integrate with a growing ecosystem of third-party tool=
s with a simple <a href=3D"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/tutorials/buildi=
ng-a-client#building-mcp-clients">client implementation</a>.</p><p class=3D=
"Body-module-scss-module__z40yvW__reading-column body-2 serif post-text">Fo=
r the remainder of this post, we'll assume each LLM call has access to thes=
e augmented capabilities.</p><h3 class=3D"Body-module-scss-module__z40yvW__=
reading-column headline-5 post-section" id=3D"workflow-prompt-chaining">Wor=
kflow: Prompt chaining</h3><p class=3D"Body-module-scss-module__z40yvW__rea=
ding-column body-2 serif post-text">Prompt chaining decomposes a task into =
a sequence of steps, where each LLM call processes the output of the previo=
us one. You can add programmatic checks (see "gate=E2=80=9D in the diagram =
below) on any intermediate steps to ensure that the process is still on tra=
